by nicolas-grekas at 2026-10-19T05:56:26Z

I pushed a fix for subclasses that implement `GlobalsInterface`. Twig rejects them only in the constructor of `AttributeExtension`, and subclasses don't have to call it. With the extension below, `{{ g }}` worked with `$twig->addExtension(new AppExtension($foo))` but was undefined once the bundle registered it:

```php
class AppExtension extends AttributeExtension implements GlobalsInterface
{
    public function __construct(private Foo $foo) {}

    public function getGlobals(): array { return ['g' => 'G']; }
}
```

These subclasses are now kept as regular extensions.

Let's merge once twigphp/Twig#4995 is merged, since this PR relies on the methods of `AttributeExtension` being final.

